  "aiContextParagraph": "The 100th iteration of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade, originally scheduled for Thursday, has been postponed to Saturday due to extreme weather conditions affecting the United States. New York City officials, including Mayor Zohran Mamdani, advised that wind gusts reaching 60 to 65 miles per hour necessitated the schedule change to ensure public safety. This event marks the first time in the parade's history that such a delay has occurred due to severe weather. Beyond the New York City region, weather disturbances are reportedly impacting other parts of the country, with snow noted in the Midwest and flood warnings issued for both the East and West coasts. These environmental factors have caused widespread disruption to holiday travel plans and traditional activities across various states, contributing to a broader national disruption during the holiday period.",
